sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant M as Mesut (Terminal, conda vla)
  participant L as webots-controller (launcher)
  participant P as python3 ders21_kol.py
  participant W as Webots.app (GUI, ders21_masa.wbt)
  Note over W: The world opens. Since Robot.controller = extern,<br/>Webots WAITS for a controller (synchronization TRUE)
  W->>W: /tmp/webots/user/PID folder (IPC channel)
  M->>L: export WEBOTS_HOME=/Applications/Webots.app<br/>$WEBOTS_HOME/Contents/MacOS/webots-controller ders21_kol.py
  L->>L: WEBOTS_CONTROLLER_URL=ipc://1234<br/>PYTHONPATH += $WEBOTS_HOME/Contents/lib/controller/python<br/>DYLD_LIBRARY_PATH += .../Contents/lib/controller
  L->>P: exec python3 -u ders21_kol.py (python3 on PATH = the vla environment)
  P->>P: import controller (libController.dylib is loaded with ctypes)
  P->>W: Supervisor() : connect over IPC to the newest Webots instance
  loop for each pose (4 times)
    P->>W: Motor.setPosition(q)
    loop 60 steps
      P->>W: robot.step(16)
      W-->>P: physics advanced 16 ms, sensors up to date
    end
    P->>W: Camera.saveImage(wrist_*.png) / exportImage(view_*.jpg)
    P->>W: getFromDef('BOWL').getPosition()
    W-->>P: world coordinates
  end
  P->>P: objects.csv, pairs.csv (robot-relative left/right/front)
  Note over M,W: It also works without the launcher: WEBOTS_HOME + PYTHONPATH by hand,<br/>python ders21_kol.py — libController finds the newest instance under /tmp/webots
